	(text_box "T-013 TX drive (D007): DRV8876 full bridge, VM = +12V boost (T-012; sequences up after 3V3_D).\nControl enters via hierarchical ports TX_EN/TX_PH/TX_NSLEEP/TX_PMODE/TX_NFAULT; the top sheet\nbridges them to the digital sheet's global labels (pinmap.md: pio1/2/48/8 out, pio5 in).\nGateware tx_nco_pwm drives tx_a->EN/IN1, tx_b->PH/IN2 -> drive TX_PMODE HIGH for IN1/IN2 (PWM)\nmode. EN/PH/nSLEEP/PMODE have internal pull-downs: bridge idles safe before FPGA is configured.\nnFAULT is open-drain; R170 pulls up to +3.3V (per pinmap.md).\nVREF = +3.3V, R171 = 1.69k -> current trip ~1.95A, far above transducer current (~50mA pk),\nso current chopping never engages. IMODE strapped to GND via R172 - CONFIRM IMODE/PMODE strap\ntables against the DRV8876 datasheet at CP-C (offline during T-013). C284 47nF CPH-CPL per\ndatasheet typical application (George's draft had 22nF - verify at CP-C).\nOff-board transducer on J50 (MKDS 5.08mm screw terminal, center-cell cable per D001/D007).\nR173/R174 = 0R 0603 series elements; swap for 0603 inductors (EMI option). R175+C288 = DNP\nsnubber provision across the transducer.\nTRANSDUCER LIMITS - enforced by gateware tx_nco_pwm, see orchestration/tx-limits.md:\nMA40S4S: 40.0kHz fixed tone ONLY, 20Vpp max continuous square (datasheet Table 1). The 12V\nbridge drives 24Vpp at full scale -> amplitude cap 187/256 (~73% duty = 20Vpp fundamental-\nequivalent). Piezo horn tweeter (20-32kHz chirps): provisional full scale OK, re-check against\nthe purchased part's datasheet before exceeding 187. Measure differential Vpp at J50 at CP-E."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 44.45 146.05 0)
		(size 128 47)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
